/*
This example script demonstrates capability of recursive script
calls on example of factorial calculation.

A call of scripts is performed with the help of 'call' function
that reads a script file and executes the script. A called
script has its own variable context that does not interfere with
a context of the calling script. The 'call' function passes the
specified parameters between variable contexts of calling and
called scripts.
*/

if (!CallLevel()) {
  // Ask for a number if the first call in the call chain
  num = NumDialog("Enter the number to calculate factorial",
                   1, 5, 1, 20);
  if (_isnan(num)) return;  // exit if cancelled
}

// recursive call for calculation of factorial
if (num <= 1) {
  factr  = 1;
}
else {
  // get file path of this script 
  script = ScriptPath();

  // call new instance of this script and
  // pass value of num-1 to it as an input value
  factr  = num * call(script, (x=num-1,"x >> num"));

// ---
// the statement above is similar to:
// x = num - 1;
// factr = num * call(script, "x >> num");
//
// in C, it can look like:
// factr = num * factorial(num-1);
// ---
}

if (!CallLevel()) {
  // Display result of calculation if the instance is
  // top-level in the call chain (i.e. calculation completed)
  msg = sform("Factorial of %d is equal to %.0f", num,factr);
  MsgBox(msg);
}
return factr;
